B.bRv=new A.fk("Box breathing relaxation technique","Sunnybrook Hospital","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tEmt1Znux58","3 min")
B.bB6=new A.fL("box","Box breathing","Four equal sides: in, hold, out, hold. Steadying and simple.",B.aPb,B.bpR,"Feeling stressed or scattered",null,3,null,"Breathing",B.bRv)
B.bdj=s(["Rest the tip of your tongue just behind your top front teeth.","Breathe out fully through your mouth.","Close your mouth and breathe in quietly through your nose for 4.","Hold your breath for 7.","Breathe out through your mouth, with a soft whoosh, for 8.","That's one breath. Do four in a row to start with."],t.s)
B.a4v=new A.id(B.Co,7)
B.a4x=new A.id(B.kU,8)
B.bro=s([B.nK,B.a4v,B.a4x],t.CM)
B.bRi=new A.fk("How to perform the 4-7-8 breathing exercise","Andrew Weil, M.D.","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YRPh_GaiL8s","2 min")
B.bB7=new A.fL("478","4-7-8 breathing","A long, slow out-breath that many people find helps them wind down.",B.bdj,B.bro,"Winding down before sleep","Feeling light-headed is common at first. If you do, stop and breathe normally; it gets easier with practice.",3,null,"Breathing",B.bRi)
B.be1=s(["Breathe in through your nose.","When your lungs feel full, take one more short sip of air in.","Breathe out slowly and fully through your mouth, longer than the in-breaths.","One to three sighs is often enough."],t.s)
B.a4w=new A.id(B.nJ,2)
B.a4z=new A.id(B.uD,1)
B.aTz=s([B.a4w,B.a4z,B.Cq],t.CM)
B.bRc=new A.fk("Reduce anxiety and stress with the physiological sigh","Andrew Huberman (Huberman Lab)","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rBdhqBGqiMc",null)
B.bBe=new A.fL("sigh","Physiological sigh","Two breaths in, one long breath out. The quickest way to settle.",B.be1,B.aTz,"A fast reset in the moment",null,3,null,"Breathing",B.bRc)
B.b39=s(["Sit or lie comfortably with a hand on your belly.","Breathe in through your nose for 5, feeling your belly rise.","Breathe out gently for 5.","Keep it smooth and unforced for 5 to 10 minutes.","Some women find slow breathing like this helps them ride out a hot flush; it's worth a try when one begins."],t.s)
B.a4A=new A.id(B.nJ,5)
B.a4B=new A.id(B.kU,5)
B.boJ=s([B.a4A,B.a4B],t.CM)
B.bRp=new A.fk("5 minute resonance breathing (6 breaths per minute)","Pocket Breath Coach - Luke Horton","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=982In66Kic8","5 min")
B.bBd=new A.fL("paced","Slow paced breathing","About six slow breaths a minute, in for 5 and out for 5.",B.b39,B.boJ,"Calming down, and when a hot flush starts",null,3,null,"Breathing",B.bRp)
B.b4k=s(["Lie down or sit comfortably and close your eyes if you like.","Take a few slow breaths and notice where your body touches the bed or chair.","Bring your attention to your toes. Notice any warmth, tingling, tightness or nothing at all.","Slowly move up: feet, ankles, calves, knees, thighs, hips.","Then your belly, chest, back, shoulders, arms and hands.","Finally your neck, jaw, face and the top of your head.","If your mind wanders, that's normal. Gently come back to where you were.","Finish with a few breaths, feeling your whole body at once."],t.s)
B.bRs=new A.fk("10 minute body scan meditation","Priory","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aH72AScs0qk","12 min")
B.bB3=new A.fL("scan","Body scan","Slowly moving your attention through your body, noticing without changing.",B.b4k,null,"Tension, and falling asleep",null,3,null,"Body scan",B.bRs)
B.bas=s(["Notice 5 things you can see.","4 things you can feel (your feet on the floor, your clothes).","3 things you can hear.","2 things you can smell.","1 thing you can taste.","Finish with one slow breath."],t.s)
B.bRt=new A.fk("The 5-4-3-2-1 method: a grounding exercise","The Partnership In Education","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=30VMIEmA114","4 min")
B.bB0=new A.fL("grounding","5-4-3-2-1 grounding","Using your senses to come back to the present moment.",B.bas,null,"Anxious or racing thoughts",null,3,null,"Meditation",B.bRt)
B.b5D=s(["Sit or lie comfortably.","Breathe in and gently tense your feet for about 5 seconds.","Breathe out and let them go completely. Notice the difference for 10 seconds.","Move up through your calves, thighs, hands, arms, shoulders and face.","Go gently: tense, don't strain, and skip anywhere that hurts."],t.s)
B.bRr=new A.fk("How to do progressive muscle relaxation","Therapist Aid","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1nZEdqcGVzo",null)
B.bBg=new A.fL("pmr","Progressive muscle relaxation","Tensing and then releasing each muscle group in turn.",B.b5D,null,"Physical tension and stress",null,3,null,"Meditation",B.bRr)
B.aDE=s(["Sit comfortably, upright but not stiff. Close your eyes or look softly at the floor.","Notice your breath wherever it's easiest to feel: the nose, the chest or the belly.","Don't change it. Just feel each breath come in and go out.","Your mind will wander. When you notice, that moment of noticing is the practice. Gently come back to the breath.","Start with 5 minutes. A few minutes most days helps more than a long session now and then."],t.s)
B.bRl=new A.fk("Five minute mindful breathing","Epworth HealthCare","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I-SFdhVwrVA","5 min")
B.bB8=new A.fL("meditation","Breath awareness meditation","Resting your attention on your breathing, and coming back when it wanders.",B.aDE,null,"A calmer mind, and starting a daily habit",null,5,null,"Meditation",B.bRl)
B.b_I=s(["Lie on your back on a bed or mat with a pillow under your knees and a blanket, so you stay warm.",'Set a simple intention, a short positive phrase such as "I am at ease".',"Move your attention slowly around the body, part by part.","Feel the breath without changing it, counting breaths down from 20.","Notice opposite feelings in turn: heavy then light, warm then cool.","Rest in stillness, repeat your intention, then come back slowly.","Falling asleep is fine; it's a sign your body needed the rest."],t.s)
B.bRe=new A.fk("15 minute yoga nidra","Ally Boothroyd | Sarovara Yoga","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nLq3XR7YlLg","18 min")
B.bBb=new A.fL("nidra","Yoga nidra (deep rest)","Lying still and following a guided rest through the body and breath.",B.b_I,null,"Poor sleep, tiredness, and an afternoon reset",null,15,null,"Yoga nidra",B.bRe)
B.bh3=s(["Have a notebook or the notes app ready.","Think back over today, even a hard day.","Write down three things that went well or that you're glad about, big or tiny: a warm drink, a kind message, a walk.","For each one, add a line on why it happened or why it mattered.","Read them back slowly and let yourself feel each one.","Doing this most evenings for a week or two is when people tend to notice a difference."],t.s)
B.bRk=new A.fk("The 3 good things exercise","Wellbeing Online","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NnB8Qr_3G4U","2 min")
B.bBf=new A.fL("gratitude","Three good things","Writing down three things that went well today, and why.",B.bh3,null,"Low mood, and ending the day on a kinder note",null,5,null,"Gratitude or journaling",B.bRk)
B.b8f=s(["Walk at an easy pace, anywhere safe: a park, a street, a garden.","Feel your feet: heel, sole, toes, each step meeting the ground.","Notice your breath and how your body moves as you walk.","Widen out to sounds, near and far, without naming them.","Then what you can see: colours, light, movement.","Then smells and the air on your skin.","When your mind wanders, come back to the feeling of your feet."],t.s)
B.bRn=new A.fk("10 minute mindful walking meditation","AXA Global Healthcare","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kapvpqwcNLQ","10 min")
B.bB9=new A.fL("walk","Mindful walk","An ordinary walk with your attention on your senses and steps.",B.b8f,null,"Busy thoughts, and getting outside",null,10,null,"Mindful walk",B.bRn)
B.aTJ=s(["Sit comfortably with your shoulders relaxed.",'Curl the sides of your tongue into a tube and poke it out a little. If you can\'t curl it, keep your lips in a small "o" with your teeth together and breathe through them.',"Breathe in slowly through the tongue or teeth for 4 and feel the cool air.","Close your mouth and breathe out gently through your nose for 6.","Repeat for 2 to 5 minutes."],t.s)
B.bRm=new A.fk("Sitali cooling breath","Yoga With Adriene","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sXai5Wvcg1M","11 min")
B.bB4=new A.fL("cooling","Cooling breath (sitali)","Breathing in over a curled tongue, then out slowly through the nose.",B.aTJ,B.L3,"A cooling, calming breath during a hot flush","Avoid it in very cold air, and stop if you feel dizzy.",3,null,"Breathing",B.bRm)
B.b6T=s(["Sit upright. Rest your left hand in your lap.","Use your right thumb to close your right nostril and your ring finger to close your left.","Close the right nostril and breathe in through the left for 4.","Close the left, open the right, and breathe out through the right for 4.","Breathe in through the right for 4, then swap and breathe out through the left.","That's one round. Keep going for 3 to 5 minutes, slow and quiet."],t.s)
B.b8H=s([B.nK,B.Cp],t.CM)
B.bRd=new A.fk("Alternate nostril breathing","Yoga With Adriene","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8VwufJrUhic","11 min")
B.bB1=new A.fL("alternate","Alternate nostril breathing","Breathing through one nostril at a time, swapping each breath.",B.b6T,B.b8H,"Balance and calm before sleep or a busy moment","If your nose is blocked, skip it for today and try slow paced breathing instead.",3,null,"Breathing",B.bRd)
B.b7G=s(["Sit comfortably and take a few slow breaths.","Bring yourself to mind and silently say: may I be well, may I be at ease, may I be kind to myself.","Think of someone you love and wish them the same.","Then someone neutral, like a shop assistant you saw today.","If you like, someone you find difficult, as far as feels OK.","Finish by wishing everyone well, yourself included."],t.s)
B.bRj=new A.fk("10-minute loving kindness meditation with Sharon Salzberg","Tricycle","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e-TeW9CI0bc","8 min")
B.bBa=new A.fL("kindness","Loving-kindness","Silently wishing yourself and others well with a few kind phrases.",B.b7G,null,"Self-criticism, irritability and low mood",null,8,null,"Meditation",B.bRj)
B.bgW=s(["Pick one small food: a raisin, a square of chocolate, a slice of apple.","Look at it as if for the first time: colour, shape, texture.","Smell it, and notice what happens in your mouth.","Put it on your tongue without chewing for a moment.","Chew slowly and notice the taste change.","Swallow, and notice the after-taste. Try one mindful bite at your next meal."],t.s)
B.bRh=new A.fk("Mindful eating exercise","ParkviewHealth","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vGGx9RhVamY","5 min")
B.bB2=new A.fL("eating","Mindful eating","Eating one small food slowly, with all your senses.",B.bgW,null,"Eating on autopilot, and enjoying food more",null,5,null,"Meditation",B.bRh)
B.b3B=s(["Sit or lie comfortably and close your eyes.","Picture a place where you feel calm and safe, real or imagined: a beach, a garden, a cosy room.","Notice what you can see there: colours, light, shapes.","Then what you can hear, what you can smell, and the temperature on your skin.","Let yourself rest there and feel how calm your body is.","Give the place a word. Saying that word later can help bring the feeling back."],t.s)
B.bRg=new A.fk("Mindful relaxation exercises: safe place imagery","Tees, Esk and Wear Valleys NHS Foundation Trust","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s0brEfm2wtk","6 min")
B.bBc=new A.fL("safeplace","Calm place visualisation","Picturing a place where you feel safe and relaxed, using every sense.",B.b3B,null,"Anxiety, and settling before sleep",null,5,null,"Meditation",B.bRg)
B.bpS=s(["Think of something that's bothering you right now, something small to start with.","Say to yourself: this is a moment of difficulty. This is hard.","Then: difficult moments are part of life. Many women feel this too.","Put a hand on your heart or wherever feels soothing.","Say: may I be kind to myself. Or ask: what do I need right now?","Take a breath and notice how you feel."],t.s)
B.bRx=new A.fk("General self-compassion break","Dr. Kristin Neff","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A7tfP1WH3_I","5 min")
