B.ba9=s(["What is menopause?","What is the difference between perimenopause and menopause?","Am I in perimenopause?","What is postmenopause?"],t.s)
B.bgJ=s(["perimenopause","stages","transition","postmenopause"],t.s)
B.bqC=s(["Perimenopause is the time leading up to menopause, when the ovaries slowly make less oestrogen and progesterone. Periods often become irregular, and symptoms like hot flashes, poor sleep or mood changes can start.","Menopause itself is one moment: 12 months in a row without a period. In Canada it happens at about 51 on average. Everything after that is called postmenopause.","The transition most often begins between 45 and 55 and usually lasts several years, about seven on average, though it can be shorter or longer."],t.s)
