B.aeF=new A.bC("what-is-perimenopause",B.k9,"What is perimenopause?",B.ba9,B.bgJ,B.bqC,null,B.aDy,B.bE)
B.beS=s(["Is there a test for menopause?","Do I need a blood test to know if I am in menopause?","What are the signs of menopause?"],t.s)
B.b3o=s(["signs","test","fsh","diagnosed","started"],t.s)
B.bdf=s(["For most women over 45, menopause is recognised from your periods and symptoms rather than a test: it has happened once you have gone 12 months without a period.","Hormone blood tests (like FSH) go up and down a lot during perimenopause, so a single result often can't say where you are. Doctors mostly use them for younger women or when the picture is unclear.","Common early signs are changes in your cycle, hot flashes or night sweats, trouble sleeping, mood changes and vaginal dryness."],t.s)
B.bdV=s([B.XD,B.XM,B.rv],t.P)
B.aex=new A.bC("am-i-in-menopause",B.k9,"How do I know if I am in menopause?",B.beS,B.b3o,B.bdf,"If your periods stop or symptoms start before 45, or you are not sure what is going on, it is worth a visit.",B.bdV,B.bE)
B.beT=s(["My periods are irregular","Why are my periods heavier?","Skipped period perimenopause"],t.s)
B.b5O=s(["period","periods","irregular","heavy","cycle","spotting"],t.s)
B.baq=s(["Yes, changing periods are usually the first sign of perimenopause. They can come closer together or further apart, be lighter or heavier, and you may skip some.","Keeping a simple note of dates and flow (the Journal works for this) makes it easier to describe to your doctor."],t.s)
B.aJl=s([B.zs,B.zi],t.P)
B.Bg=new A.f4(B.r8,null,4,"iron")
B.ng=new A.f4(null,"ferritin",16,"ferritin")
B.b5L=s([B.Bg,B.ng],t.G)
B.aey=new A.bC("periods-changing",B.k9,"Is it normal for my periods to change?",B.beT,B.b5O,B.baq,"See your doctor for very heavy bleeding (soaking a pad or tampon every hour or two), periods lasting more than about a week, bleeding between periods or after sex, or any bleeding once periods have stopped for 12 months.",B.aJl,B.b5L)
B.bmj=s(["Spotting after my periods stopped","Postmenopausal bleeding","Bleeding after a year with no period"],t.s)
B.bpg=s(["postmenopausal","spotting","bleeding","bleed"],t.s)
B.b3l=s(["Any bleeding or spotting once you have gone 12 months without a period should be checked by a doctor, even if it is light or happens only once.","Most of the time the cause is something simple, like thin, dry tissue or a polyp, but bleeding after menopause can sometimes be an early sign of cancer of the uterus, which is very treatable when found early."],t.s)
B.b6M=s([B.zi,B.zx],t.P)
B.aeU=new A.bC("bleeding-after-menopause",B.k9,"I have bleeding after menopause. Is that normal?",B.bmj,B.bpg,B.b3l,"Book an appointment soon rather than waiting to see if it stops.",B.b6M,B.bE)
B.b7e=s(["When will hot flashes stop?","Will this ever end?"],t.s)
B.b6U=s(["long","last","years","stop","end"],t.s)
B.b3F=s(["It is different for everyone. Hot flashes and night sweats often last several years, around seven on average, and some women have them for longer. Others have very few.","Many symptoms, like brain fog and sleep trouble, tend to ease after the transition. Some changes, like vaginal dryness and bone loss, can continue, which is why looking after bones, heart and pelvic health matters long term."],t.s)
B.b5F=s([B.mM,B.zw,B.Xh],t.P)
B.aeK=new A.bC("how-long-symptoms",B.k9,"How long do menopause symptoms last?",B.b7e,B.b6U,B.b3F,"If symptoms are affecting your work, sleep or relationships, you do not have to wait them out: there are effective treatments.",B.b5F,B.bE)
B.bo2=s(["How do I stop hot flushes?","Ways to cool down during a hot flash","Natural remedies for hot flashes"],t.s)
B.b4D=s(["flash","flashes","flush","flushes","heat","cool"],t.s)
B.bpF=s(["Simple things help many women: dress in layers you can take off, keep a fan or cold drink nearby, and notice your own triggers. Common ones are alcohol, caffeine, spicy food, hot drinks, stress and warm rooms.","Slow, paced breathing when a flash starts can take the edge off (the hot flash breathing practice in Mindfulness is made for this). Cognitive behavioural therapy (CBT) and clinical hypnosis also have good evidence.","For flashes that really get in the way, hormone therapy is the most effective treatment, and there are non-hormonal prescription options too. These are worth a conversation with your doctor."],t.s)
B.b7z=s([B.zq,B.mM,B.zu],t.P)
B.a02=new A.f4(null,null,23,"mindfulness")
B.xB=s([B.a02],t.G)
B.aee=new A.bC("hot-flashes",B.dZ,"What helps with hot flashes?",B.bo2,B.b4D,B.bpF,"Talk to your doctor if hot flashes disturb your sleep or daily life.",B.b7z,B.xB)
B.bq0=s(["I wake up soaked","Sweating at night","Too hot in bed"],t.s)
B.bd4=s(["sweat","sweats","sweating","soaked","drenched","night"],t.s)
B.b7i=s(["Night sweats are hot flashes that happen while you sleep. A cool bedroom, a fan, light breathable sheets and nightwear, and layers you can throw off all help.","Keep cold water by the bed, and try to avoid alcohol, big meals and spicy food in the evening, since they are common triggers.","If they wake you most nights, the same treatments that help hot flashes (including hormone therapy) usually help night sweats."],t.s)
B.b8A=s([B.mM,B.Xl],t.P)
B.aeS=new A.bC("night-sweats",B.dZ,"How can I cope with night sweats?",B.bq0,B.bd4,B.b7i,"Night sweats with fever, weight loss you can't explain, or that started outside the usual menopause years should be checked.",B.b8A,B.bE)
B.blm=s(["Does spicy food cause hot flashes?","Does wine make hot flashes worse?"],t.s)
B.bgE=s(["trigger","triggers","spicy","wine","alcohol","coffee"],t.s)
B.aRm=s(["The most common triggers are alcohol (especially red wine), caffeine, spicy food and hot drinks. Smoking and stress can make them worse too.","Triggers are personal. Noting when flashes happen in the Journal for a week or two, alongside your food log, can show whether any of these matter for you."],t.s)
B.b3M=s([B.rx,B.mM],t.P)
B.aeV=new A.bC("hot-flash-triggers",B.dZ,"Which foods trigger hot flashes?",B.blm,B.bgE,B.aRm,null,B.b3M,B.bE)
B.b8Z=s(["Memory problems during menopause","I can't concentrate","Trouble finding words"],t.s)
B.brF=s(["fog","memory","forget","forgetful","concentrate","focus"],t.s)
B.bru=s(["Brain fog, forgetfulness and trouble concentrating are common in perimenopause. Changing hormones play a part, and so do poor sleep and stress. For most women it improves after the transition.","Things that help: better sleep (and treating night sweats that break it), regular movement, lists and reminders, and doing one thing at a time."],t.s)
B.bqH=s([B.k8,B.rv],t.P)
B.aez=new A.bC("brain-fog",B.dZ,"Why do I have brain fog and forget things?",B.b8Z,B.brF,B.bru,"If memory problems are getting worse, worrying you or your family, or come with other changes, see your doctor.",B.bqH,B.bE)
B.b4H=s(["Stiff joints in the morning","Achy muscles menopause"],t.s)
B.aRe=s(["joint","joints","ache","aches","achy","stiff","stiffness"],t.s)
B.bhw=s(["Aching, stiff joints are a common and often overlooked menopause symptom, as oestrogen helps with inflammation and joint comfort.","Gentle regular movement, strength work, stretching, staying at a healthy weight and sleep all help. Warmth can ease morning stiffness."],t.s)
B.aDn=s([B.k8,B.XS],t.P)
B.tE=new A.f4(null,null,21,"movement")
B.xV=s([B.tE],t.G)
B.af2=new A.bC("joint-aches",B.dZ,"Why do my joints ache?",B.b4H,B.aRe,B.bhw,"See your doctor if a joint is red, hot or swollen, if pain is severe, or if it does not improve.",B.aDn,B.xV)
B.bdm=s(["Heart palpitations","Pounding heart at night"],t.s)
B.b3r=s(["palpitations","racing","flutter","fluttering","pounding"],t.s)
B.b8_=s(["Palpitations (a racing, pounding or fluttering heartbeat) are common around menopause, often with hot flashes. Caffeine, alcohol, stress and poor sleep can set them off.","They are usually harmless, but because heart disease risk rises after menopause, new palpitations are worth mentioning to your doctor."],t.s)
B.b8u=s([B.XL,B.ry,B.ru],t.P)
B.aeC=new A.bC("palpitations",B.dZ,"Why does my heart race or flutter?",B.bdm,B.b3r,B.b8_,"Call 911 if palpitations come with chest pain, shortness of breath, fainting or feeling very unwell. Otherwise see your doctor if they are new, frequent or last a long time.",B.b8u,B.bE)
B.aDx=s(["My migraines are worse","More headaches lately"],t.s)
B.beL=s(["headache","headaches","migraine","migraines"],t.s)
B.b8U=s(["Yes. Shifting hormone levels can make headaches and migraines more frequent in perimenopause. For many women who had hormone-linked migraines, they ease after menopause.","Regular meals, enough water, steady sleep, and keeping an eye on caffeine and alcohol help. A headache diary can show patterns."],t.s)
B.b_C=s([B.XI,B.XF,B.mN],t.P)
B.aeP=new A.bC("headaches",B.dZ,"Can menopause cause headaches or migraines?",B.aDx,B.beL,B.b8U,"Get help right away (call 911) for a sudden, very severe headache, or one with weakness, confusion, trouble speaking or a drooping face. See your doctor if headaches change or get worse.",B.b_C,B.bE)
B.b6n=s(["Itchy skin menopause","Hair loss menopause","Dry eyes"],t.s)
B.blA=s(["skin","itchy","dry","hair","thinning","eyes","nails"],t.s)
B.b8W=s(["Lower oestrogen means skin makes less collagen and oil, so dryness, itchiness and thinner skin are common. Hair can thin too, and some women notice dry eyes.","A gentle fragrance-free moisturiser, sunscreen, enough protein and healthy fats, and drinking enough water help."],t.s)
B.bdk=s([B.k8,B.XC,B.Xm,B.Xx],t.P)
B.Bi=new A.f4(null,"tsh",20,"tsh")
B.bfd=s([B.ng,B.Bi],t.G)
B.aeY=new A.bC("skin-hair",B.dZ,"Why is my skin dry and my hair thinning?",B.b6n,B.blA,B.b8W,"See your doctor for sudden or patchy hair loss, or itching with a rash; it can be checked for things like thyroid or iron problems.",B.bdk,B.bfd)
B.blG=s(["Menopause belly","How do I lose weight during menopause?","Why is my weight going up?"],t.s)
B.b8d=s(["weight","belly","middle","waist","gain","lose","fat"],t.s)
B.brZ=s(["Lower oestrogen shifts where the body stores fat, towards the waist, and muscle is slowly lost with age, which lowers the calories you burn. Poor sleep and stress add to it.","What helps most is building and keeping muscle (strength work twice a week and protein at each meal), plenty of fibre, regular activity, and good sleep. Small steady changes work better than strict diets."],t.s)
B.bgH=s([B.XH,B.rw,B.rA],t.P)
B.tC=new A.f4(B.el,null,0,"protein")
B.nf=new A.f4(B.dX,null,3,"fiber")
B.nh=new A.f4(null,null,22,"strength")
B.b5t=s([B.tC,B.nf,B.nh],t.G)
B.aeN=new A.bC("weight-gain",B.dZ,"Why am I gaining weight around my middle?",B.blG,B.b8d,B.brZ,null,B.bgH,B.b5t)
B.b92=s(["Bloating and gas","Constipation menopause","Upset tummy"],t.s)
B.bkc=s(["bloat","bloated","bloating","gas","constipation","constipated","digestion"],t.s)
B.b5y=s(["Bloating is common around menopause, as hormone changes affect digestion and fluid. Constipation can add to it.","Raising fibre slowly (with more water), eating regular meals, moving every day and noticing foods that bother you (fizzy drinks, some beans or onions, sweeteners like sorbitol) often help."],t.s)
B.b93=s([B.Xg,B.XX,B.zh],t.P)
B.M7=s([B.nf],t.G)
B.aev=new A.bC("bloating",B.dZ,"Why do I feel bloated?",B.b92,B.bkc,B.b5y,"See your doctor if bloating is there most days for three weeks or more, or comes with weight loss, blood in your stool, changes in bowel habits or feeling full quickly.",B.b93,B.M7)
B.bfW=s(["Light-headed","Feeling faint"],t.s)
B.b5h=s(["dizzy","dizziness","lightheaded","faint","vertigo"],t.s)
B.b3J=s(["Some women feel dizzy or light-headed around menopause, sometimes with hot flashes or palpitations. Not drinking enough, skipping meals, standing up quickly and low iron can also cause it."],t.s)
B.aLH=s([B.Xq,B.mN],t.P)
B.Bh=new A.f4(null,"hemoglobin",17,"hemoglobin")
B.akK=s([B.Bh,B.ng],t.G)
B.aeL=new A.bC("dizziness",B.dZ,"Why do I feel dizzy?",B.bfW,B.b5h,B.b3J,"Call 911 if dizziness comes with chest pain, a drooping face, weakness or trouble speaking. See your doctor if it keeps happening.",B.aLH,B.akK)
B.b9g=s(["I can't sleep","Insomnia during menopause","Trouble falling asleep"],t.s)
B.bdv=s(["sleep","insomnia","asleep","bedtime","rest"],t.s)
B.brD=s(["Sleep problems are very common in menopause, from night sweats, needing the bathroom, worry and hormone changes.","Steady habits help: the same wake-up time every day, a cool, dark bedroom, no caffeine after lunch, less alcohol, daylight and movement during the day, and winding down without screens.","Cognitive behavioural therapy for insomnia (CBT-I) is the first treatment experts recommend for long-term insomnia, and it works well. Treating night sweats often helps sleep too."],t.s)
B.bm4=s([B.zr,B.zn,B.XU,B.XV],t.P)
B.aeG=new A.bC("sleep-better",B.il,"How can I sleep better?",B.b9g,B.bdv,B.brD,"See your doctor if poor sleep lasts more than a few weeks, or if you snore loudly or stop breathing in your sleep (sleep apnoea becomes more common after menopause).",B.bm4,B.xV)
B.boG=s(["Waking up during the night","I wake up and can't get back to sleep"],t.s)
B.b6p=s(["wake","waking","awake","3am","night"],t.s)
B.b5Y=s(["Waking in the night is a classic menopause complaint. Night sweats, a full bladder, a racing mind and lighter sleep with age all play a part.","If you can't get back to sleep after about 20 minutes, get up and do something quiet in dim light until you feel sleepy. Slow breathing or a body scan can help. Cutting back on fluids and alcohol in the evening helps with bathroom trips."],t.s)
B.bnK=s([B.zr,B.zn,B.Xu],t.P)
B.af8=new A.bC("waking-at-night",B.il,"Why do I wake up at 3 am?",B.boG,B.b6p,B.b5Y,"Restless, uncomfortable legs at night, or loud snoring, are worth mentioning to your doctor.",B.bnK,B.xB)
B.b59=s(["Mood swings menopause","I feel on edge","Anxiety during perimenopause"],t.s)
B.b5C=s(["anxiety","anxious","irritable","mood","moods","swings","angry","worry","panic"],t.s)
B.bka=s(["Mood changes, anxiety and irritability are common in perimenopause. Changing hormones affect brain chemicals, and poor sleep and life stress add up.","Regular movement, time outdoors, connecting with people, cutting back on alcohol and caffeine, and calming practices like slow breathing help many women. CBT works well for anxiety and for menopause symptoms."],t.s)
B.aRr=s([B.k8,B.zy,B.Xi,B.Xe],t.P)
B.bgs=s([B.a02,B.tE],t.G)
B.af_=new A.bC("anxiety-mood",B.il,"Why do I feel anxious or irritable?",B.b59,B.b5C,B.bka,"If anxiety or low mood is there most days, see your doctor. Both hormone and non-hormone treatments can help.",B.aRr,B.bgs)
B.b3Y=s(["I feel sad all the time","Depression and menopause","I feel hopeless"],t.s)
B.aRf=s(["depressed","depression","sad","low","hopeless","crying","tearful","down"],t.s)
B.bom=s(["The risk of depression goes up during perimenopause, even for women who have never had it before. It is not a weakness, and it is treatable.","Talking to someone you trust, staying active, keeping a routine, and getting help early all make a difference."],t.s)
B.b96=s([B.zk,B.Xj,B.k8],t.P)
B.aes=new A.bC("low-mood",B.il,"I feel low or depressed. What can I do?",B.b3Y,B.aRf,B.bom,"See your doctor if you have felt low most days for two weeks or more. If you are thinking about suicide or harming yourself, call or text 9-8-8 any time, or call 911.",B.b96,B.xV)
B.b2U=s(["I have no energy","Always exhausted","Fatigue"],t.s)
B.baD=s(["tired","fatigue","exhausted","energy","drained","sluggish"],t.s)
B.bgu=s(["Tiredness in menopause often comes from broken sleep (night sweats, waking early), plus stress and hormone changes.","It is also worth ruling out other common causes: low iron or anaemia, an underactive thyroid, low vitamin B12, and some medicines. A simple blood test can check these.","Regular meals with protein and fibre, enough water, daylight and gentle activity usually help energy more than rest alone."],t.s)
B.boI=s([B.Xz,B.zz,B.zp],t.P)
B.a00=new A.f4(null,"b12",18,"b12Blood")
B.b3I=s([B.ng,B.Bh,B.Bi,B.a00,B.Bg],t.G)
B.aeo=new A.bC("tired",B.il,"Why am I so tired all the time?",B.b2U,B.baD,B.bgu,"See your doctor if you are tired for more than a few weeks without a clear reason.",B.boI,B.b3I)
B.b4c=s(["I feel overwhelmed","Ways to relax"],t.s)
B.biR=s(["stress","stressed","overwhelmed","relax","calm","tension"],t.s)
B.aTG=s(["Stress can make hot flashes, sleep and mood worse, and midlife often brings a lot of it at once.","A few minutes a day of slow breathing, meditation or yoga, regular movement, time outside, saying no sometimes, and talking things through all help. Small, regular habits work better than an occasional big effort."],t.s)
B.awT=s([B.zy,B.zu],t.P)
B.aeM=new A.bC("stress",B.il,"How can I manage stress?",B.b4c,B.biR,B.aTG,null,B.awT,B.xB)
B.bk2=s(["How do I prevent osteoporosis?","Bone loss menopause","Strong bones"],t.s)
B.b9U=s(["bone","bones","osteoporosis","fracture","density"],t.s)
B.aDA=s(["Bone loss speeds up for several years after menopause because oestrogen helps protect bone. That is why osteoporosis is much more common in women after 50.","The basics: enough calcium (mostly from food), vitamin D, enough protein, strength and balance exercise, not smoking and keeping alcohol low."],t.s)
B.b4j=s([B.XT,B.zg,B.zj],t.P)
B.tD=new A.f4(B.re,null,1,"calcium")
B.Bf=new A.f4(B.r7,null,2,"vitaminD")
B.b7I=s([B.tD,B.Bf,B.nh],t.G)
B.aet=new A.bC("bones",B.h1,"How do I look after my bones after menopause?",B.bk2,B.b9U,B.aDA,"Ask your doctor about your fracture risk and whether you need a bone density test, especially if you have broken a bone from a minor fall, or a parent broke a hip.",B.b4j,B.b7I)
B.b8o=s(["Should I take calcium?","Calcium foods","Calcium supplement"],t.s)
B.blt=s(["calcium","dairy","milk","cheese","yogurt"],t.s)
B.b67=s(["Women over 50 need about 1,200 mg of calcium a day in total. Osteoporosis Canada suggests getting it from food first, and only topping up with a supplement if food falls short.","Good sources: milk and fortified plant drinks (about 300 mg a cup), yogurt, cheese, canned salmon or sardines with the bones, tofu made with calcium, almonds, and some greens.","Osteoporosis Canada has a free calcium calculator to estimate what you get from food."],t.s)
B.bki=s([B.zt,B.XP],t.P)
B.b4x=s([B.tD],t.G)
B.af6=new A.bC("calcium",B.h1,"How much calcium do I need?",B.b8o,B.blt,B.b67,"Check with your doctor or pharmacist before starting a calcium supplement, especially if you have had kidney stones.",B.bki,B.b4x)
B.aDp=s(["How much vitamin D do I need?","Vitamin D in winter"],t.s)
B.b7Y=s(["vitamin","sun","sunshine","winter","d"],t.s)
B.bnX=s(["Vitamin D helps your body use calcium. In Canada the sun is too weak to make enough for much of the year, and few foods have much.","Canada's food guide recommends that adults over 50 take a daily vitamin D supplement of 400 IU, on top of eating foods with vitamin D (milk and fortified plant drinks, fatty fish, eggs). Osteoporosis Canada gives the total daily amount from food and supplements as 600 IU up to age 70 and 800 IU after."],t.s)
B.b8O=s([B.zA,B.rt],t.P)
B.bRW=new A.f4(null,"vitamin_d",19,"vitaminDBlood")
B.aX4=s([B.Bf,B.bRW],t.G)
B.af0=new A.bC("vitamin-d",B.h1,"Should I take vitamin D?",B.aDp,B.b7Y,B.bnX,"Ask your doctor or pharmacist which amount is right for you, especially at higher doses.",B.b8O,B.aX4)
B.b47=s(["What is a DEXA scan?","BMD test"],t.s)
B.aRv=s(["dexa","bmd","scan","density","test"],t.s)
B.b90=s(["A bone mineral density (BMD) test is a quick, painless scan that measures bone strength and helps work out your fracture risk.","Osteoporosis Canada suggests it for everyone 70 and over, for women after menopause aged 65 to 69 with one risk factor, and for those 50 to 64 who have broken a bone in a minor fall or have two or more risk factors (such as a parent with a hip fracture, long-term steroid use, low body weight, smoking or early menopause)."],t.s)
B.bqQ=s([B.XQ,B.zg],t.P)
B.aeH=new A.bC("bone-density-test",B.h1,"Do I need a bone density test?",B.b47,B.aRv,B.b90,"Your doctor can tell you whether you should have one and when.",B.bqQ,B.bE)
B.bqc=s(["Protein ideas for breakfast","Am I eating enough protein?","Protein for muscle"],t.s)
B.blw=s(["protein","muscle","breakfast","eggs","beans","meat"],t.s)
B.bcT=s(["Protein helps keep muscle and bone as you age. The basic guideline for adults is 0.8 g per kg of body weight a day, and many experts suggest a little more (about 1.0 to 1.2 g per kg) for women over 50, especially if you are active.","Spreading it across the day helps: some protein at every meal, including breakfast. Greek yogurt, eggs, milk, tofu, beans, lentils, nuts, fish and chicken are all good choices, and Canada's food guide encourages plant proteins often."],t.s)
B.bqw=s([B.Xv,B.k7],t.P)
B.akY=s([B.tC],t.G)
B.aeT=new A.bC("protein",B.h1,"How much protein do I need?",B.bqc,B.blw,B.bcT,"If you have kidney disease, check with your doctor before eating more protein.",B.bqw,B.akY)
B.ban=s(["Weights after 50","Exercises for bones","How do I keep muscle?"],t.s)
B.b5B=s(["strength","weights","resistance","muscle","lifting","gym"],t.s)
B.bbz=s(["Yes, it is one of the best things you can do in midlife. Strength work keeps muscle, protects bones, helps balance and blood sugar, and makes everyday tasks easier.","The Canadian guidelines suggest muscle-strengthening on at least two days a week. Bands, light weights, body-weight moves (sit-to-stand, wall push-ups) or Pilates all count. Osteoporosis Canada adds balance work and good posture."],t.s)
B.b89=s([B.rA,B.zj,B.rw],t.P)
B.aTH=s([B.nh],t.G)
B.aeu=new A.bC("strength-training",B.h1,"Should I do strength training?",B.ban,B.b5B,B.bbz,"If you have osteoporosis or a past fracture, ask for advice on safe moves (a physiotherapist can help).",B.b89,B.aTH)
B.b7_=s(["Is walking enough?","Exercise guidelines","How active should I be?"],t.s)
B.b7F=s(["exercise","active","activity","walking","walk","minutes","fitness"],t.s)
B.aJ4=s(["The Canadian 24-Hour Movement Guidelines suggest about 150 minutes a week of moderate to vigorous activity (like brisk walking), strength work on two days, and less time sitting. Adults 65+ are also encouraged to do balance exercises.","Walking is a great start. Adding a few hills, some brisk stretches and two short strength sessions a week covers most of it. Every bit counts, even 10 minutes at a time."],t.s)
B.b32=s([B.rA,B.Xf,B.rw],t.P)
B.bjK=s([B.tE,B.nh],t.G)
B.aeh=new A.bC("how-much-exercise",B.h1,"How much exercise do I need?",B.b7_,B.b7F,B.aJ4,null,B.b32,B.bjK)
B.bja=s(["Heart disease risk after menopause","Protect my heart"],t.s)
B.b9_=s(["heart","cardiovascular","heart disease"],t.s)
B.bgZ=s(["Yes. Oestrogen helps protect blood vessels, so after menopause the risk of heart disease rises, and it is the leading cause of death for women. LDL cholesterol and blood pressure often go up in these years.","The good news is that most of the risk can be changed: move every day, eat lots of vegetables, fruit, whole grains, beans and nuts, limit salt and saturated fat, don't smoke, keep alcohol low, and know your blood pressure, cholesterol and blood sugar numbers."],t.s)
B.aXa=s([B.ru,B.zw,B.rs],t.P)
B.a01=new A.f4(null,"ldl",12,"ldl")
B.a_X=new A.f4(B.mB,null,7,"satFat")
B.a_Y=new A.f4(B.rb,null,6,"sodium")
